WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.564
This is how to create single

00:00:01.564 --> 00:00:03.240
word captions in Premiere Pro.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.631
Start by heading to the Workspaces options

00:00:05.631 --> 00:00:07.680
and selecting Captions and Graphics.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.982
Come up to Text, make sure your audio

00:00:11.982 --> 00:00:14.240
is selected and then choose Transcribe.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.008
Premiere will transcribe your

00:00:16.008 --> 00:00:18.080
audio and generate the transcript.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.242
Check that everything is correct,

00:00:20.242 --> 00:00:21.880
then click the CC button.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.920
This will open up this window.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.240
Under Layout, click Single Word

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.560
and then click Create Captions.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:30.317
And now you have single word

00:00:30.317 --> 00:00:31.760
captions in your video.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.503
To customise your text, select all the captions,

00:00:34.503 --> 00:00:36.160
head to the Properties panel,

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.900
where you'll find controls for the Transform,

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.240
Font, Size and Colour.
